From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:44:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 327/342] DHCPClient: ask for broadcast answers while there is
 no lease

When a C2's lease from a wireless bridge ended with the bridge
gone, the router NAKed its renewal and the client discovered again every
minute or so, with the bridge's address still on the interface. The
router answered each DISCOVER within 4 ms with an offer sent to the
offered address, and IPv4 dropped every one: it takes a unicast for an
address the interface doesn't have only on an interface without any
address (and sends back host unreachable). The board kept using a NAKed
address with no lease.

In INIT, SELECTING, REQUESTING, INIT-REBOOT and REBOOTING the client now
sets the BROADCAST flag, as RFC 2131 4.1 has a client do that can't take
such unicasts, so the offer and the ACK come as broadcasts. Renewing and
rebinding, which have an address, are unchanged.

tools/dhcp-moved-test.sh on the test board's cable (a 60 s lease, then a
router that NAKs it and offers another address): on +334 the board looped
for 100 s on the old address, never seeing an offer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp b/src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp
index 06e1552343..869721eca7 100644
--- a/src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/net/DHCPClient.cpp
@@ -1046,6 +1046,18 @@ DHCPClient::_PrepareMessage(dhcp_message& message, dhcp_state state)
 		/ 1000000LL, 65535));
 	memcpy(message.mac_address, fMAC, 6);
 
+	// Without a lease, ask for the answers as broadcasts (RFC 2131 4.1).
+	// Sent to the offered address, they would be dropped while the
+	// interface still has another one (IPv4 takes a unicast for an address
+	// it doesn't have only on an interface without any): a lease that has
+	// ended, a NAK, a move to another network. A C2 on Wi-Fi kept a bridge's
+	// lease that way when the bridge was gone, never seeing the router's
+	// offers.
+	if (state == INIT || state == SELECTING || state == REQUESTING
+		|| state == INIT_REBOOT || state == REBOOTING) {
+		message.flags = htons(DHCP_FLAG_BROADCAST);
+	}
+
 	message_type type = message.Type();
 
 	uint8 *next = message.PrepareMessage(type);
